  "instruction": "Claude r23 (2026-09-28): the affinity figures (design ingame/설계_v3_글메뉴판.md 「r23 요구」). Codex must never run publish_calendar_*.py --restore, publish_modmenu_*.py --restore, publish_chart_*.py --restore or publish_feeling_*.py --restore or otherwise remove the calendar overlay (KR_T9*/KR_T17*/KR_T18*/KR_T19*/KR_T20* functions, the nine r15 same-length operands, the RunEvent operand swap in KR_T9HomeCasual, the seven r20 same-length operands in C_Status::RunStatus, C_HomeStatusView@SetInfo, C_SceneTraining@RunSelectPartner and C_SceneTraining@_UpdateInputPartner), the mod-menu request consumer (KR_M* functions and the two r21 same-length operands: KR_T9HomeMenuRun calls KR_MHomeRun where it called ■選択ダイアログ／実行, C_SelectDialog@_Update calls KR_MTick where it called C_UserInputManager::IsClickEnterOtherMouse) or the event flow chart (KR_C* functions, the six r22 one-call forwarders KR_MDo -> KR_CDoHome, KR_T9Seen -> KR_CSeen, KR_T9State -> KR_CState, KR_T9Legend -> KR_CLegend, KR_T18CardPage -> KR_CCardPage, KR_T18EventPage -> KR_CEventPage, and the two r22 same-length operands: C_SceneTitle@Update calls KR_CTitleTick where it called C_UserInputManager::IsClickConfig, C_SceneTitle@Run calls KR_CTitleServe where it called ■方向キー処理／削除) or the affinity figures (KR_T23* functions and the three r23 same-length operands: C_HomeStatusView@SetActivePage asks KR_T23FeelShow where it asked IsShowFeelingPage, C_FeelingView@1 calls KR_T23FvGone where it called DeleteMarks, KR_T20StActiveOf calls KR_T23StDraw where it called KR_T20StDraw). The calendar, the mod menu, the chart and the affinity figures are permanent user-requested features: when a rebuild needs a clean base, rebase on the runtime that current.json points to and carry the calendar, mod-menu, chart and affinity functions forward; restore is reserved for the user's explicit request. Payload: NightRemaster.ain only; PACT/EX/FNL, the Manual chart and winmm.dll untouched. KR_T23* functions appended (tables baked: the 28 feeling_gate triggers of graph/schedule.json with the last day each can fire); no original function relocated, no forwarder; no new global / struct member / session variable; no save schema change. Values are the game's own: C_Ability@GetFeeling (m_nFeeling / GetFeelingRate), the maximum 120 = C_FeelingView@Update's 60 a moon x at most two moons, the rank = C_SysVoice::GetFeelingRank_5 + 1 (bounds 15 / 30 / 45 / 60 inclusive). Three same-length operand swaps: C_HomeStatusView@SetActivePage PUSH C_HomeStatusView@IsShowFeelingPage -> KR_T23FeelShow (CALLMETHOD target: the original query, then the moon text part 2026092330 made / released under the status root exactly when the moons are shown: IsShowFeelingPage and m_FeelingView.Enabled(m_CharaNo)), C_FeelingView@1 (the destructor) PUSH C_FeelingView@DeleteMarks -> KR_T23FvGone (the original DeleteMarks, then the moon text part released: nothing is left when a status view dies), KR_T20StActiveOf CALLFUNC KR_T20StDraw -> KR_T23StDraw (the r20 「이벤트」 page; a person with moons gets 「친밀도 v (r/5) · 다음 조건 n」 + the gate's r19 name + the 「루트」 line right under the title and a taller panel; everyone else r20's page exactly). <runtime>/KRMenu/ is the temporary exchange-file folder of the mod-menu hook and the game script (request.txt, last_result.txt, reset.req, restore.req): never put it in a manifest, ignore it in every tree check, and never delete it (a pending reset.req / restore.req or an unread last_result.txt may be waiting there). Pinned (index, address and every code byte identical): KR_T9HomeCasual, KR_T9HomeConfig, C_SceneHomebase@CheckGameSysButtons, C_SceneHomebase@Run, LSys3xScript::RunEvent, KR_T18RunSandboxed. r15's nine, r18's one, r20's seven, r21's two and r22's two same-length sites and r18's eight / r19's five / r22's six forwarders stay. Every earlier contract stays in force.",
